Bananas had asked his friend about his golden naga problem, and
Hippoctes
 had given him this advice: "While those silver scales that you're
wearing look
good, those grey scales that you came back with would work much
better."
So Bananas took off his silver scales (he still hadn't found out which
scroll
was enchant armour) and put on his grey scales instead.

"All this shopping and smiting is making me tired.  Ah! A nice looking
seat.
I think I'll sit down for a while." *poof!* "Congratulations sir!
You're the 200th
person to sit in this seat! You've won a prize of your choice!"
Bananas missed
 his sparkly blingy silver armour, so he asked for the next best thing.
 A shiny
silver amulet.  "Consider it done!"  So Bananas put on his mirrorlike
amulet
and felt much safer from random lightning strikes.

Hippocrates had told Bananas that there was "something special" about
his
walking stick, so Bananas decided to try it out.  Amazingly, when he
hit his
 enemies with it, they seemed to become weaker.  This seemed like a
pretty
 powerful ability, so Bananas read his two remaining enchant weapon
scrolls
 to power up the staff (+4).  Bananas killed a wraith and it left a
corpse.  This
was a dilemma for Bananas.  He was already satiated, but wraith corpses

were so tasty "you can't eat just one!"  He cast remove sickness once
to
make room in his belly, then ate the corpse.  All of a sudden he felt
sensitive.
 Hooray! (Side note: Did casting a spell help me avoid choking?)

In a throne room (about dungeon level 20), Bananas finally found a
scroll of
enchant armour, and was able to upgrade his grey dragon scales to scale

mail.  He also alchemised up about 20 blessed full healing potions and
quaffed 15 of them.  Feeling much healthier, Bananas continued
downward.
Soon he came to a small island, and could see a little building on
another
 island nearby.  So he quaffed a potion of levitation and floated over
to the
small building.  He had heard that a hideous snake haired woman lived
inside
the building.  He didn't want to look at something that was so scary,
so he
wrapped a towel around his head and walked inside.  He took off his
towel,
 but didn't see anything scary, just a few statues.

Bananas wanted a way to get back and forth over the water easily, and
the
 boots on one of the statues looked fairly funky, but he had no pickaxe
to
smash it with.  He looked through his wands, and found a wand of
striking!
"I'll zap that statue until it's just little rocks!" *pbbbtt!* "Oh
crap! My only
wand of striking and it's empty.  Maybe if I try really hard it will
work one last
 time" *pbbbtt!* *pbbbtt!*... (several minutes later...) *pbbbtt!*
*Zap!*
"Huzzah! I broke the statue... and there's nothing but rocks here...
*sigh*"

Down again, and into a maze.  A master liche gave him a lot of trouble
teleporting over, fighting and teleporting away again to heal.  His
walking
stick wasn't doing enough damage, so he switched back to the vorpal
blade to fight the liche.  This tactic paid off and the very sharp
blade
eventually decapitated his foe.

Soon enough, he came to a large castle with the drawbridge up.  He
couldn't figure out how to get in, so he decided to busk with his
bugle,
to earn some extra zorkmids.  All of a sudden, the drawbridge came
down and monsters started crossing the moat.

To be continued in part 3... (yes I am stretching out this YASD or YAAP
out a bit)
